ご視聴ありがとうございました

21
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:29,500
Mankind cannot live alone.

22
00:02:29,620 --> 00:02:31,720
Although you, yourself, are always unique.

23
00:02:31,920 --> 00:02:33,220
That is why life is hard.

24
00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:35,200
That is why life is sad and empty.

25
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:38,340
Thus you want the close physical and mental presence of others.

26
00:02:38,520 --> 00:02:40,160
That is why we wish to become one.

27
00:02:40,620 --> 00:02:43,600
The human soul is made of weak and fragile elements.

28
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:46,340
The body and mind are made of brittle components as well.

29
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:51,300
And so, via the instrumentality, mankind must fill and complement each other.

30
00:02:51,820 --> 00:02:52,600
Must you ask?

31
00:02:52,860 --> 00:02:54,640
Because there's no other way to exist.

32
00:02:54,640 --> 00:02:59,040
Why do you exist?

33
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:02,920
Maybe I exist to find out why I exist.

34
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:04,560
For whom do you exist?

35
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:06,580
For myself, of course.

36
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:09,160
Maybe for myself.

37
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:12,460
Are you happy being alive?

38
00:03:12,780 --> 00:03:13,580
I don't know.

39
00:03:13,980 --> 00:03:15,760
Are you happy being alive?

40
00:03:16,180 --> 00:03:17,460
Of course I'm happy!

41
00:03:18,020 --> 00:03:20,020
Are you happy being alive?

42
00:03:20,220 --> 00:03:22,340
I don't want to do anything except to be happy.

43
00:03:22,720 --> 00:03:23,920
Do you hate being sad?

44
00:03:24,640 --> 00:03:25,960
I don't like it.

45
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:28,300
Do you hate enduring pain?

46
00:03:28,980 --> 00:03:30,020
I don't like it.

47
00:03:30,460 --> 00:03:31,840
Is that why you run away?

48
00:03:32,280 --> 00:03:32,640
Yes.

49
00:03:33,080 --> 00:03:33,800
Do you blame me?

50
00:03:34,220 --> 00:03:36,520
What's wrong with running away from something that hurts?

51
00:03:36,860 --> 00:03:37,860
I mustn't run away.

52
00:03:38,180 --> 00:03:39,800
Tell me why you mustn't run away.

53
00:03:39,980 --> 00:03:42,000
Because escaping from reality can be painful.

54
00:03:42,100 --> 00:03:44,160
Even though you're running from something more painful?

55
00:03:44,740 --> 00:03:45,900
I couldn't bear it.

56
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:48,780
As long as you know what the pain is, it can be endured.

57
00:03:49,120 --> 00:03:49,820
That's correct.

58
00:03:50,260 --> 00:03:52,180
If the pain is too harsh, you can escape it.

59
00:03:52,620 --> 00:03:55,460
If you really hate it, Shinji, you can still run.

60
00:03:56,120 --> 00:03:57,120
No, I won't.

61
00:03:57,380 --> 00:03:58,380
I'm tired of escaping.

62
00:03:58,380 --> 00:04:01,620
Yes, I mustn't run away.

63
00:04:01,900 --> 00:04:02,680
That is true.

64
00:04:03,060 --> 00:04:06,060
That is because you are now aware that running only brings you more pain.

65
00:04:06,300 --> 00:04:08,800
This is because running away can be far worse.

66
00:04:08,960 --> 00:04:10,860
That's why you do not wish to escape.

67
00:04:11,400 --> 00:04:13,660
Because if you run away, nobody will respect you.

68
00:04:14,640 --> 00:04:15,780
Don't leave me alone.

69
00:04:16,440 --> 00:04:17,260
Don't deserve me.

70
00:04:17,300 --> 00:04:18,040
I'm begging you.

71
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:21,320
There he goes again, depending upon others who do everything for him.

72
00:04:21,800 --> 00:04:23,940
That's a sad survival mechanism, isn't it?

73
00:04:23,940 --> 00:04:24,620
So what?

74
00:04:25,100 --> 00:04:26,880
It's better than being left all alone.

75
00:04:27,320 --> 00:04:28,880
Because you fear being hurt.

76
00:04:29,360 --> 00:04:31,800
You try to make yourself believe that, don't you?

77
00:04:32,620 --> 00:04:34,700
You're not the only one who gets hurt, Shinji.

78
00:04:35,080 --> 00:04:36,440
Everybody feels pain.

79
00:04:36,720 --> 00:04:38,000
You aren't the only one.

80
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:41,120
It's just easier for you to think that it's true, isn't it?

81
00:04:41,660 --> 00:04:42,320
Shut up!

82
00:04:42,580 --> 00:04:43,400
I don't care!

83
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:44,600
Why should I?

84
00:04:44,820 --> 00:04:46,080
Nobody cares about me!

85
00:04:46,440 --> 00:04:49,800
Once again, you've abandoned all sense of self-value, of self-worth.

86
00:04:50,580 --> 00:04:51,380
I have nothing.

87
00:04:51,380 --> 00:04:52,300
I have nothing.

88
00:04:52,300 --> 00:04:55,760
There you go again, saying that you have no worth at all.

89
00:04:56,060 --> 00:04:59,060
Do you believe that by not expecting anything, you won't get hurt either?

90
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:01,760
Is that how you sustain your pathetic ego?

91
00:05:02,000 --> 00:05:03,760
By asking others to praise you?

92
00:05:04,180 --> 00:05:05,340
Nobody accepts me.

93
00:05:05,660 --> 00:05:06,620
That's not true.

94
00:05:06,760 --> 00:05:08,120
You just believe that is so.

95
00:05:08,580 --> 00:05:10,460
And so that's why I must pilot the Ava.

96
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:12,320
Again, that is merely your point of view.

97
00:05:12,660 --> 00:05:15,580
You've been trying to convince yourself that you're worthless since the very beginning.

98
00:05:15,640 --> 00:05:16,440
But I have to!

99
00:05:16,780 --> 00:05:17,980
I've got to do it!

100
00:05:18,360 --> 00:05:19,560
No, that's not true.

101
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:20,780
You don't have to.

102
00:05:20,780 --> 00:05:22,460
No, you just think you do.

103
00:05:22,900 --> 00:05:23,680
No, you're wrong.

104
00:05:24,340 --> 00:05:25,900
My life is pointless otherwise.

105
00:05:26,500 --> 00:05:28,400
And that's why you pilot the Ava?

106
00:05:28,940 --> 00:05:31,440
Piloting Ava gives me an identity, a purpose.

107
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:34,920
Piloting Ava gives me an identity, a purpose.

108
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:38,200
I had no value before I became a pilot.

109
00:05:38,680 --> 00:05:41,760
The fact that I now pilot an Ava justifies my presence here.

110
00:05:41,760 --> 00:05:44,260
I have no other value.

111
00:05:44,700 --> 00:05:46,100
I have no other value.

112
00:05:46,400 --> 00:05:47,860
I have no other value.

113
00:05:48,180 --> 00:05:49,640
No other value at all.

114
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:53,620
I perceive no value in myself.

115
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:56,400
I hate myself.

116
00:05:57,800 --> 00:05:59,080
You little worm!

117
00:05:59,280 --> 00:06:00,020
I hate you!

118
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:00,920
I hate you!

119
00:06:01,380 --> 00:06:02,220
Me too!

120
00:06:02,440 --> 00:06:03,440
I hate you too!

121
00:06:03,440 --> 00:06:05,440
I hate everything about you!

122
00:06:05,440 --> 00:06:07,440
I'm sorry, but I hate you!

123
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:09,440
I hate you!

124
00:06:09,440 --> 00:06:11,440
I hate you.

125
00:06:11,440 --> 00:06:13,440
I hate you.

126
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:15,440
I hate everything about you.

127
00:06:15,440 --> 00:06:17,440
I hate you.

128
00:06:17,440 --> 00:06:19,440
Oh, Shinji, I hate you.

129
00:06:19,440 --> 00:06:21,440
See? Everyone hates me!

130
00:06:21,440 --> 00:06:23,440
Every person in existence must hate me!

131
00:06:23,440 --> 00:06:25,440
No, that's just what you imagine.

132
00:06:25,440 --> 00:06:29,440
Yes! But that must be it, because I hate myself!

133
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:32,440
Because you hate yourself, no one respects you.

134
00:06:32,440 --> 00:06:34,440
I hate you! I hate you!

135
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:36,440
I hate everything!

136
00:06:36,440 --> 00:06:38,440
They praise me.

137
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:40,440
They're nice to me.

138
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:44,440
When I pilot the Ava, they treat me better.

139
00:06:44,440 --> 00:06:48,440
Other people are being nice to me for the first time.

140
00:06:48,440 --> 00:06:50,440
Which is your true feeling?

141
00:06:50,440 --> 00:06:54,440
I don't know. Or is it perhaps that both are my true feelings?

142
00:06:54,440 --> 00:06:56,440
So that's why you pilot the Ava?

143
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:59,440
Because I have no choice. I only have the Ava.

144
00:06:59,440 --> 00:07:01,440
Otherwise, you could not retain your own identity.

145
00:07:01,440 --> 00:07:04,440
In fact, Ava Unit 1 is part of your sense of being.

146
00:07:04,440 --> 00:07:09,440
But if you depend only on the Ava, then the Ava will become your only identifier.

147
00:07:09,440 --> 00:07:11,440
Ava will become your only value.

148
00:07:11,440 --> 00:07:15,440
Without that value, you, the real you, will be erased from this existence.

149
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:19,440
I don't care. I had no other value to start with anyway.

150
00:07:19,440 --> 00:07:22,440
I was learning to play the cello, but that didn't help me either.

151
00:07:22,440 --> 00:07:25,440
You just didn't discipline yourself. I didn't have to do that.

152
00:07:25,440 --> 00:07:27,440
But now that I can pilot the Ava...

153
00:07:27,440 --> 00:07:33,440
No. Soon you may lose your identity, as I have. Soon you may lose Ava and your self-worth.

154
00:07:33,440 --> 00:07:35,440
I pilot it because that's all I can do.

155
00:07:43,440 --> 00:07:50,440
Rain. Dark shadows of gloom hang above me. That's how I feel. This isn't how I want it to be.

156
00:07:50,440 --> 00:07:56,440
The setting sun. The ending of life. This is not how I wish it to be.

157
00:07:56,440 --> 00:08:04,440
Morning. The beginning of a day. Another terrible day. I wish this wasn't the way it is.

158
00:08:04,440 --> 00:08:12,440
Blue sky. Something warm. Something unfamiliar. Something that fills me with horror.

159
00:08:12,440 --> 00:08:14,440
I don't want this. I don't want it to be this way.

160
00:08:14,440 --> 00:08:16,440
I hate everything!

161
00:08:16,440 --> 00:08:18,440
What do you want, Shinji?

162
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:20,440
What do you want, Shinji?

163
00:08:20,440 --> 00:08:22,440
What do you want, Shinji?

164
00:08:22,440 --> 00:08:24,440
What do you want, Shinji?

165
00:08:24,440 --> 00:08:26,440
Don't let me please!

166
00:08:26,440 --> 00:08:28,440
What I fear is...

167
00:08:28,440 --> 00:08:30,440
What I want is...

168
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:32,440
Can I stay next to you?

169
00:08:32,440 --> 00:08:34,440
May I stay here?

170
00:08:34,440 --> 00:08:36,440
Do you like me?

171
00:08:40,440 --> 00:08:42,440
Do you want to go where your mother is?

172
00:08:42,440 --> 00:08:43,440
No.

173
00:08:43,440 --> 00:08:46,440
Don't you want to go be with your father?

174
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:48,440
No, I don't.

175
00:08:48,440 --> 00:08:50,440
Why?

176
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:52,440
Because I'm afraid of being hated.

177
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:56,440
Because my identity might start to disappear.

178
00:08:56,440 --> 00:08:58,440
What is it that you wish for?

179
00:08:58,440 --> 00:09:00,440
What is it that you want?

180
00:09:00,440 --> 00:09:02,440
What is it that you want?

181
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:04,440
You're very insecure, aren't you?

182
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:08,440
To become secure, I have to have value.

183
00:09:08,440 --> 00:09:10,440
I want to be worth something.

184
00:09:10,440 --> 00:09:14,440
I want to be worth enough to attract the attention of others.

185
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:18,440
But your value is something you have to find for yourself.

186
00:09:18,440 --> 00:09:20,440
You have to find it, Shinji.

187
00:09:20,440 --> 00:09:22,440
I have no value without it.

188
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:24,440
My life is worthless without it.

189
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:28,440
Then what am I?

190
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:30,440
Then what am I?

191
00:09:30,440 --> 00:09:32,440
What am I?

192
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:34,440
Wait, what is this?

193
00:09:34,440 --> 00:09:36,440
This is me.

194
00:09:36,440 --> 00:09:38,440
This is the shape that lets others recognize me as myself.

195
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:40,440
It is my symbol for myself.

196
00:09:40,440 --> 00:09:41,440
This is...

197
00:09:41,440 --> 00:09:42,440
This is...

198
00:09:42,440 --> 00:09:43,440
And this is as well.

199
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:44,440
Representations.

200
00:09:44,440 --> 00:09:47,440
Everything is merely a description, not the real myself.

201
00:09:47,440 --> 00:09:51,440
Everything is simply a shape, a form, an identifier to let others recognize me as me.

202
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:53,440
But then, what am I?

203
00:09:53,440 --> 00:09:54,440
Is this me?

204
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:55,440
My true self?

205
00:09:55,440 --> 00:09:56,440
My fake self?

206
00:09:56,440 --> 00:09:57,440
What is it that I am?

207
00:09:57,440 --> 00:09:58,440
You are you.

208
00:09:58,440 --> 00:10:03,440
There is little difference between how you interpret yourself and how the others interpret you.

209
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:04,440
Right.

210
00:10:04,440 --> 00:10:05,440
My clothes.

211
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:06,440
My shoes.

212
00:10:06,440 --> 00:10:07,440
My room.

213
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:10,440
These are all parts of what makes up myself.

214
00:10:10,440 --> 00:10:13,440
These things are connected through your consciousness.

215
00:10:13,440 --> 00:10:15,440
So what I think is me, is me.

216
00:10:15,440 --> 00:10:18,440
What I recognize as self, is myself.

217
00:10:18,440 --> 00:10:21,440
I'm no more and no less than the sum of my self-awareness.

218
00:10:21,440 --> 00:10:23,440
But I don't understand myself.

219
00:10:23,440 --> 00:10:24,440
Where am I?

220
00:10:24,440 --> 00:10:25,440
What am I?

221
00:10:25,440 --> 00:10:26,440
What am I?

222
00:10:26,440 --> 00:10:27,440
What am I?

223
00:10:29,440 --> 00:10:32,440
Nobody understands me!

224
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:34,440
What are you, stupid?

225
00:10:34,440 --> 00:10:36,440
Of course nobody understands you.

226
00:10:36,440 --> 00:10:39,440
Nobody can ever understand you.

227
00:10:39,440 --> 00:10:43,440
The only one who can take care of you and understand you is...

228
00:10:43,440 --> 00:10:45,440
You, yourself.

229
00:10:45,440 --> 00:10:47,440
So you must take care of yourself.

230
00:10:48,440 --> 00:10:50,440
But I still don't understand myself.

231
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:53,440
I don't even know what it is that makes me myself.

232
00:10:53,440 --> 00:10:54,440
How could I love myself?

233
00:10:54,440 --> 00:10:57,440
You are still unstable.

234
00:10:57,440 --> 00:10:59,440
That is the present you.

235
00:10:59,440 --> 00:11:01,440
And the people around the present you.

236
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:04,440
And the environment that surrounds the present you.

237
00:11:04,440 --> 00:11:08,440
None of these elements of reality last forever.

238
00:11:08,440 --> 00:11:11,440
Time continues to flow and time brings change.

239
00:11:11,440 --> 00:11:14,440
Your world is in a state of constant change.

240
00:11:14,440 --> 00:11:18,440
You are capable of change anytime your mind perceives these changes.

241
00:11:18,440 --> 00:11:20,440
What is this?

242
00:11:20,440 --> 00:11:22,440
A world of nothing?

243
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:24,440
A world with nobody in it?

244
00:11:24,440 --> 00:11:26,440
This is the world of perfect freedom.

245
00:11:26,440 --> 00:11:27,440
Freedom?

246
00:11:27,440 --> 00:11:28,440
Perfect freedom.

247
00:11:28,440 --> 00:11:30,440
A world in which you have no restriction.

248
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:33,440
A world in which you have no restriction.

249
00:11:33,440 --> 00:11:34,440
Is this really freedom?

250
00:11:34,440 --> 00:11:35,440
Yes.

251
00:11:35,440 --> 00:11:37,440
This is what it is.

252
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:39,440
However, this world has nothing in it.

253
00:11:39,440 --> 00:11:41,440
Unless I do something?

254
00:11:41,440 --> 00:11:42,440
Right.

255
00:11:42,440 --> 00:11:44,440
Unless you do or think of something.

256
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:47,440
But I don't know what to do or think of.

257
00:11:47,440 --> 00:11:48,440
He is uncertain.

258
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:51,440
He has no self-image to orient himself.

259
00:11:51,440 --> 00:11:52,440
There's nothing solid here.

260
00:11:52,440 --> 00:11:55,440
It is a world in which there are no obstacles.

261
00:11:55,440 --> 00:11:56,440
No anything.

262
00:11:56,440 --> 00:11:59,440
This is a world in which you can do anything you wish.

263
00:11:59,440 --> 00:12:02,440
And yet, you are still afraid, aren't you?

264
00:12:02,440 --> 00:12:04,440
Don't you know what it is that you want to do?

265
00:12:04,440 --> 00:12:05,440
